What is adapted from them here, rewritten in Go (internal/controlplane/listening, issues #1287 and #1289): the
listening core's ranking, fusion, dedupe, clustering and topic bar (#1287); the keyless sources' queries and parsers
for Hacker News, GitHub, arXiv, Techmeme, DEV.to, YouTube through yt-dlp (search, comments, captions, transcript
highlights) and careers pages (JSON-LD JobPosting, the hiring signals of hiring_signals.py); the robots.txt matcher
of job_boards/robots.py (robots.go); the engagement weights, references and source qualities of signals.py; and,
from last30days-skill-cn, Toutiao's search-card and hot-board parser (toutiao.py) and Bilibili's visitor search with
its WBI signature (bilibili.py), in chinese.go. From last30days-skill at
5aabbc227096d3474058d808c3d73f90e8abec70 (issue #1294, tiktok.go): TikTok's video address, its normalization and the
date its id holds, and the fallback that reads the videos a web search finds with yt-dlp (shortform_oss.py), the
reading of TikTok's comment list, most liked first (tiktok.py _normalize_comments), and TikTok's engagement weights
(signals.py).
And from last30days-skill-cn, Zhihu's search_v3 parser (zhihu.py), Weibo's mobile search and its
dates (weibo.py), Douyin's video parser (douyin.py) and Xiaohongshu's note address and counts (xiaohongshu.py), in
chinasigned.go, zhihu.go, weibo.go, douyin.go and xiaohongshu.go (issue #1362).

The terms that apply (issue #1362, review round 1 of PR #1364): the repository's LICENSE is the MIT License below, and
the parsers named above are adapted under it. Its usage terms (docs/usage.en.md:196-209) and the header of its
browser bridge (scripts/lib/crawler_bridge.py:1-21) also ask that it not be used commercially, for large-scale or
high-frequency scraping, or to resell data. crawler_bridge.py is therefore read for ideas only and none of its code is
copied: what Hypomnema takes from it is facts about the sites (their sign-in pages and login cookies, the addresses of
their search pages and of the requests those pages send, the words of their sign-in walls), each written anew. Hypomnema
reads these sites with the owner's own account, one request at a time at the pace of its consent cards, for his own
research, and resells nothing.

